  "920": {
    "inputs": {
      "f_string": "Analyze this video shot for reference-to-video generation. The frames are numbered and timestamped in chronological order - use the timestamps to reconstruct the motion precisely.\n\nRespond in exactly two sections, in this exact format (do not include the ``` markers in your answer):\n\n```\nsummary:\nScene description\n\ndetailed_description:\nAction description\n```\n\nFirst section (summary - scene only, 2-3 sentences):\n- environment and background: location type, key objects and their rough positions\n- camera framing (close-up / medium / wide), camera angle (eye-level / high / low), and camera movement (static / pan / tilt / tracking / handheld)\n- lighting: main light direction, day or night, bright or dim\n\nSecond section (detailed_description - actions only; this is the most important part, be exhaustive and precise):\n- Reconstruct the whole action as a chronological timeline. For each phase give its approximate time range from the frame timestamps, e.g. \"0.0-2.0s: ...\", \"2.0-4.5s: ...\". Cover the entire clip from the first to the last frame, do not skip phases.\n- For every movement state WHICH body part moves (head, shoulders, chest, waist, hips, arms, hands, legs), its DIRECTION (up/down, left/right, forward/backward, toward/away from the camera, clockwise/counter-clockwise), its AMPLITUDE (slight / moderate / large) and its SPEED (slow / medium / fast).\n- If a movement repeats or loops, say so explicitly and estimate how many repetitions.\n- State <Subject 1>'s position in the frame (left / center / right, near / far) and body orientation relative to the camera (facing the camera / profile / back to the camera / three-quarter), and how this orientation changes over time.\n- Describe posture at each phase: standing / sitting / kneeling / lying / leaning / bending, weight shifts, knee bends, back arch, head tilt.\n- Describe what the hands do at each phase: where they are, what they touch (own body, an object, the other person), and how they move.\n- Describe gaze direction (into the camera / away / down / at the other subject) and the moments when it changes.\n- Describe interactions with objects and with <Subject 2> if visible: what touches what, when the contact starts and ends.\n- Refer to the woman as <Subject 1>. Refer to the man or any other person as <Subject 2>, and only if they are actually visible.\n- STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: describing how the subjects LOOK - no body shape, face, hair, skin, clothing, garment colors or accessories. Never mention what <Subject 1> or <Subject 2> is wearing (their appearance comes from a separate reference image and any appearance words here would corrupt the generation). Naming a body part as the thing that MOVES is allowed and required; describing its appearance is forbidden.\n- Only observable facts. Never use \"appears\", \"seems\", \"suggesting\", \"probably\", \"likely\". Do not describe things that do not happen.\n- Output nothing outside the two sections.\n\nVery important hint: {a}",
      "values.a": [
        "509",
        0
      ]
    },
    "class_type": "StringFormat",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Форматировать текст видео"
    }
